<title>BELGIUM: BBL buys small Belgian bank SEFB from French GAN.</title>
<headline>BBL buys small Belgian bank SEFB from French GAN.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Banque Bruxelles Lambert (BBL) bought a majority stake in SEFB-Record Bank from French group GAN/CIC, SEFB said in a statement on Tuesday.</p>
<p>SEFB is a small Liege-based regional bank with 40 employees and assets worth 8.7 billion Belgian francs. It focuses on consumer credit. BBL has assets worth 3,440 billion francs and employs 10,800 people.</p>
<p>A spokesman for BBL declined to detail the size of the stake or the amount paid for it.</p>
